        example: 'Immediate rewards alone average to H: 0.8×2+0.2×(−1)=1.4, U: 0.9×1+0.1×(−2)=0.7, and mixture: 1.12. Including the future produces 4.288, showing explicitly the immediate and tail contributions.',
        why: 'Evaluation versus improvement runs through dynamic programming, SARSA, Q-learning and Actor–Critic; see [Sutton and Barto](https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262039246/reinforcement-learning/). Quality cost can have its own Bellman relation, but has not been mixed into this energy reward.',
