    intuition: 'SARSA and Q-learning differ in which future behavior their target describes, not whether they run in real time. SARSA evaluates the policy generating the trajectory; Q-learning’s one-step target assumes a greedy next choice under current estimates. Separate who generates data from whose behavior is evaluated to understand on-policy and off-policy.',
